<title>KENYA: Kenya produces 25.5 mln kilos of tea in May.</title>
<headline>Kenya produces 25.5 mln kilos of tea in May.</headline>
<dateline>MOMBASA, Kenya 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kenya produced 25,499,054 kg of tea in May an increase of 2,502,278 kg over the same month last year, Africa Tea Brokers (ATB) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Kenya's production for 1997 stands at 80.47 million kg, a decrease of 35.96 million over the previous year.</p>
<p>Wet, cold weather inhibited tea crop intake, the ATB said in a report.</p>
<p>Four weekly sales were held in  May and 241,117 packages were sold at an average price of $1.93.</p>
<p>The report said larger quantities were available at auction, so prices declined, particularly in the final sale.</p>
<p>However, good medium and below neat leaf Brokens were comparatively buoyant.</p>
</text>
